# LINE ENDINGS ARE LF, IN THE REPOSITORY AND IN THE WORKING TREE.
#
# Not a style preference. This repository is developed on Windows and read by contributors who are meant to be
# anywhere, and CRLF has already cost real time here twice:
#
#   · LICENSE and app/index.html drifted to CRLF, and the document that described grafting this history onto
#     the remote's had to argue about which copy of the LICENSE should win the conflict — 661 lines that
#     differed in nothing but their line endings;
#   · a multi-line search-and-replace written with `\n` matches ZERO lines in a CRLF file. It does not fail; it
#     reports success having changed nothing. A mutation that is never applied leaves the test suite green, and
#     the green means nothing.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises on commit AND checks out LF, so the second failure cannot come back. If it ever
# has to be relaxed for one path, relax it for that path and say why here — not by deleting this line.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary types that must never be normalised. None is tracked today (the engine's fonts and the browser
# tests' screenshots are both gitignored), and they are declared in advance because the day one arrives is the
# day somebody notices it was corrupted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.ogg  binary
*.wav  binary
*.onnx binary
